{
  "id": "T-31",
  "question": "Does it stop at the edge damage, or go on falling at the rim?",
  "bible": "§11",
  "gameVersion": "44.1.4.1",
  "reports": [
    {
      "on": "2026-11-25",
      "words": "I didn't have the waypoint between the feet, it's not possible to do it between, I will do one at the enemy's feet. 200 Runner, Carmine Penta, only Adhesive Blast. Screenshots are attached. Grenades were placed from the position where the distance turned from 2-3m and where it turned from 6-5m and 3 between."
    },
    {
      "on": "2026-11-25",
      "words": "Yes, 200 Runner and all the other conditions apply. The hidden was 151 and 86."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A level 200 Runner, paused in the Simulacrum, and no numbers were predicted to Pavel. The numbers were read off five screenshots, one for each row of grenades: 256, 429 (yellow), 151; 279, 218, 157, 77; 287, 491 (yellow), 173, 86; 269, 211, 148; 547 (yellow), 224, 154. They are taken to be at 2, 2.75, 3.5 and 4.25 m, in steps. An explosion counts up to the enemy's body, which is about half a metre out from where the distance is taken to. Placed by eye, so the tolerance is about a third of a metre. The wiki's straight line to the edge damage is far off near the rim. Adhesive Blast only makes the grenades stick, so it is left out. Carmine Penta is not in the library yet. ",
